# AGENT DIRECTIVES

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- Framework: Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript.
- UI: Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Lucide Icons.
- Database & Auth: Supabase (Server Client + Client Component patterns using @supabase/ssr).

## Coding Standards
1. Write clean, modular, typed TypeScript. Avoid `any`.
2. Keep components small and functional. Prefer Server Components by default.
3. Use `shadcn/ui` components located in `@/components/ui`.
4. Always handle error states, loading skeletons, and edge cases gracefully.
5. NEVER hardcode secrets or API keys. Always read from `process.env`.
6. Enforce strict Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) on all new database tables.

## Execution Rules
- Before writing major features, break down the plan in 3 bullet points.
- Do not touch existing unrelated files unless explicitly asked.
- After making changes, verify that imports are clean and types match.